+//   engine; ControlCore is the first. Everything above the interface -
+//   TermControl, tabs, panes, settings - is unaware of which one it holds.
+//
+// - Ownership runs the other way round from ControlCore. WT keeps the
+//   connection and therefore the pty (ADR 0006): output bytes arrive on the
+//   connection's thread and go into libghostty through
+//   ghostty_surface_write_pty_output, and the terminal's input comes back out
+//   through the engine's write callback into ITerminalConnection::WriteInput.
+//   libghostty spawns nothing.
